\f1\fs22 There were no fights over the lyrics; they had been written by the kids themselves and the High Elvis put the words out that they should be respected as a sign of friendship and unity. \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Gerry Hardman stood in the secure laboratory beneath a secure building securely across the road from TRAMPS Tower, watching technicians in hazmat suits make final adjustments to what resembled ordinary air filtration units. \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93You\'92re certain about effective coverage?\'94 Gerry asked the lead engineer, a nervous man with thinning hair who adjusted his protective goggles almost as often as he pulled at his underwear elastic.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Yes, Commissioner. The TMinusVirus dispersal extend approximately two hundred meters from each deployment point, covering the entirety of the plaza.\'94 The scientist gestured to a holographic map where red circles indicated coverage zones. \'93Wind conditions are favourable.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Gerry nodded, his face betraying nothing of his internal calculations. He\'92d spent the previous night reviewing and revising his recommendation to deploy. The original plan had targeted isolated Elvi communities, not a mixed crowd of Airborne, Cloudborne, and Evolution Elvi protesters.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93And the genetic targeting?\'94 he asked.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Functioning as designed. The virus will only activate in subjects with Elvi genetic markers. Others will experience mild cold-like symptoms at worst\'97useful cover for explaining the public health response.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>CEO Dunhilton\'92s voice crackled over the laboratory speakers. \'93Gerry, I\'92m looking at real-time satellite footage. They\'92re setting up portable shower facilities now. Shower facilities! They\'92re planning to stay indefinitely. I want this handled today.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Gerry looked at the engineer for confirmation. The engineer shook his head.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Your Supreme Corporateness,\'94 Gerry replied, his tone betraying no hesitation despite the accelerated timeline. \'93The gas is ready now, and the delivery devices will be fully primed tomorrow.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Dunhilton allowed an uncomfortable silence to stretch long enough for Gerry to contemplate his inevitable demise. \'93What of the press release, Gerry?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Ready and approved. We\'92re calling it a bacterial outbreak as a result of the unsanitary conditions in the encampment. The Department of Health is standing by to cordon off the area once symptoms manifest.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93But only the Elvi will be affected, right? Won\'92t that raise suspicion?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93The old Grayling clone tech  is infamous for is poor gene copying. The Elvi are cursed with tragically flawed genes. They don\'92t tend to live long anyway.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Good cover, Gerry. I like it.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Yes, Your Supreme Corporateness.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The connection terminated with an abrupt click. Gerry took an under-Layer passage back to TRAMPS Tower. From his office, he had a clear view of the protest below. It was organising and settling, seemingly every couple of hours\'97Gerry could make out sleeping areas, medical stations, food distribution, portaloos and the shower blocks Dunhilton had complained about. Most had drifted farther west along the plaza as the crowd watching the acts on stage grew.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl220\sb220\qj\partightenfactor0

