\f1\fs22 Early the next morning, the virus was deployed. Gerry returned to his window later in the afternoon at the time he was told that symptoms would be noticeable. He observed with clinical detachment. According to the briefing, symptoms would be mild at first, then increasingly severe for those with the targeted genetic markers. For the Elvi, it would progressively shut down cellular functions, presenting initially as flu-like symptoms before rapidly accelerating toward organ failure. For everyone else, it would cause minor respiratory irritation at most\'97an acceptable level of collateral spill.\
